    <ele>41.0</ele>
    <name>Gaviota SP - NIGHT 2 alt (16 km earlier)</name>
    <desc>Where CA-1 meets US-101 at the coast, under the railway trestle. Hike-and-bike campsites confirmed; drinking water, restrooms/showers, camp store. Open August 2026, reservable via ReserveCalifornia. (805) 968-1033. Stops day 2 at 285 km instead of 303 km, at the cost of a longer day 3. Known to be windy. SRC parks.ca.gov Gaviota page  [day2_limekiln_refugio km 285]</desc>
    <sym>Campground</sym>
    <type>camp</type>
  </wpt>
